WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.009
If you want to hear three theories about the
setup for a sequel, then stick around to the

00:00:04.009 --> 00:00:04.880
end of this video.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:14.360
Michael Myers, Jason, Freddy, Pennywise, Leatherface
and many others have just welcomed a new member

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:18.150
to their exclusive club of horror icon remakes
and that member is Chucky.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.480
Today on Things You Missed I’ll be covering
everything you might have missed in the 2019

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:22.660
Child’s Play.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:26.470
The new film is very different from the original,
but it’s absolutely loaded with nods and

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:30.390
parallels to the original Child’s Play series,
many of which I think you’ll be surprised

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.390
to learn.

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:34.470
The movie begins with this introduction video
to this company Kaslan, who are very similar

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:38.380
to Play Pals Toys from the original series,
in that they produce the doll and all sorts

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:39.380
of accessories.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.230
In fact, we see the inside of the factory
where the Buddi dolls are produced and it’s

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:46.470
very similar visually to the factory that
Chucky chases Kyle and Andy through in Child's

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:47.470
Play 2.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:50.030
It is here that we discover the origin of
Chucky’s evil.

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:54.140
This time it’s not a serial killer transferring
his evil soul into the body, but rather, a

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:57.980
factory worker programming his evil intentions
into the source code of this toy.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:01.290
The worker later throws himself off the building
and lands on a car for the first death of

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:02.290
the movie.

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:05.690
Aunt Maggie lands on a car for the first death
in the original Child’s Play.

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:08.960
When Andy’s mom comes home from work, the
IT guy is installing cameras in the halls

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:13.570
made by Kaslan, so it seems like they control
almost all technology in this world, but I’ll

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.030
come back to that later in this video.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:19.180
In both this and the original, Andy’s Mom
gets the doll second hand, in the original

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:22.490
it’s a street peddler and now it’s a returned
item to the store she works at.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:25.830
The name of the doll has been changed from
Good Guys to Buddi, but don’t worry, this

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:29.390
isn’t a betrayal of the original, it’s
actually a reference to the real world doll

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:31.930
that the original is based on: the My Buddy
doll.

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:36.770
Legend says that 80s kids still have the jingle
stuck in their heads and so will you after

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:37.840
I roll it!

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:40.720
“My Buddy.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:42.400
My Buddy!

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.820
Wherever I goes, he goes...”

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:48.560
The name change also just works well with
modern tech’s strange gravitation towards

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:49.560
lower case i’s.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:54.240
I guess it’s supposed to stand for internet,
but after being overused in every tech product,

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.820
I think we can agree that it stands for insufferable.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:00.660
Andy’s Mom tells him to go make friends
with some kids standing outside, but he says

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:04.370
he doesn’t want to, they could be serial
killers, a little nod to the fact that in

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:06.960
the original, the Good Guy doll is possessed
by a serial killer.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.729
Also, there’s a possible connection in that
Andy likes to draw these strange Buddy Cop

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:14.370
pairings in his notebook -- could be a reference
to the two cops who help take down Chucky

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:15.810
in the 1988 film.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:18.230
Errr… at least one of them helps.

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:21.760
In this version, the kids are given the opportunity
to give a custom name to their toy.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.760
Andy names his Han Solo.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:27.640
Big missed opportunity to not go with Luke
Skywalker instead, seeing as how Chucky is

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.900
voiced by the man who plays Luke Skywalker.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:34.280
There’s also a song known as The Buddi song
that goes: “You are my Buddi, until the

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:35.280
end.”

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.130
The original Chucky doesn’t sing, but he
does have a phrase that goes: “we’re friends

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:39.130
to the end.”

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:42.200
"Hi, I'm Oscar and I'm your friend to the
end!"

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.599
OK -- so the next part is what I find the
most interesting, because this remake has

00:02:45.599 --> 00:02:50.110
its own plot that isn’t similar to the original
but the overarching idea is the same, but

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:51.110
in a modern setting.

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:54.190
What I’m talking about is the fact that
Chucky’s voodoo possession of the doll in

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:58.599
the 1988 movie causes him to slowly become
human, but in the 2019 remake, he’s just

00:02:58.599 --> 00:03:03.480
an AI with safety restrictions removed, but
he learns how to behave by watching and imitating

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.480
the humans.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.970
So in a sense, he’s slowly becoming human
throughout the movie, because he’s learning

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:08.770
to behave like a human.

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:12.650
Unfortunately, the humans he’s taking his
cues from are irresponsible pre-teens who

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:16.959
teach him to do bad stuff for laughs, so Chucky
begins to see this as acceptable behaviour.

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:21.220
They also show him The Texas Chainsaw Massacre
2, which causes Chucky to remove one of his

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:26.050
victims’ faces, and is probably influenced
by other horror movies, judging from the posters

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:30.180
on the kid’s wall like Killer Klowns from
Outer Space and Poltergeist III, both of which

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:33.700
came out in 1988, the same year as the original
Child’s Play.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:37.790
One aspect of the new story is that Andy is
given Chucky as an early birthday present

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:40.560
because his Mom knows the move has been hard
on him.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.950
There’s also a point later where he gives
a gift to the neighbor, Mrs. Norris and tells

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.320
her they can open gifts together on his birthday.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.819
So there’s a looser connection here to Andy
from the original, who receives the Good Guy

00:03:49.819 --> 00:03:51.770
doll as a last minute birthday gift.

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:55.239
Now this next one, I don’t know if it would
count as a Thing You Missed -- maybe more

00:03:55.239 --> 00:03:57.660
of a disturbing thing that I thought about
after the fact…

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:01.720
I’m just not gonna start a whole web-series
called Disturbing Things I Thought About After

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:06.640
The Fact… but Chucky starts by killing Andy’s
cat, and that night Chucky stands in his room

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:08.430
and plays back cat noises.

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:12.239
These were probably the sounds of the cat’s
final moments, a pretty messed up soundtrack

00:04:12.239 --> 00:04:13.250
to fall asleep to.

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:17.909
I think I’ll stick with lofi chillhop beats
to study/relax/sleep for my bedtime music

00:04:17.909 --> 00:04:18.909
choices.

00:04:18.909 --> 00:04:22.719
Chucky’s next victim is Karen’s boyfriend
Shane, because for some reason all guys who

00:04:22.719 --> 00:04:26.039
date a single mother in movies turn out to
be evil -- like seriously -- try to name one

00:04:26.039 --> 00:04:27.270
exception to this rule.

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:30.789
He’s taking down Christmas lights when Chucky
finds him, which tells us that this movie

00:04:30.789 --> 00:04:34.260
still takes place in January like the original
despite the fact that it seems to be in a

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:37.039
warm-weather climate as opposed to Chicago.

00:04:37.039 --> 00:04:40.020
Taking down the lights was a neat way to show
this without drawing too much attention to

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.400
an otherwise unnecessary detail.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:46.669
Chucky attacks him in a very similar way to
how Aunt Maggie is attacked with Chucky rushing

00:04:46.669 --> 00:04:50.219
around in the dark before knocking his victim
down from a high up place.

00:04:50.219 --> 00:04:54.210
He tears Shane’s face off and his hair lands
on a garden gnome, which instantly made me

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:59.249
think of this Keemstar video from 2016 where
he wears an emo wig and pretends to be LeafyIsHere.

00:04:59.249 --> 00:05:00.920
“I want to kill myself.”

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:03.000
"Also in the news."

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:07.639
When Andy and his friends realize that Chucky
has gone too far, they take steps to deactivate

00:05:07.639 --> 00:05:11.099
it and they do so by removing, what I’m
assuming is supposed to be the battery, which

00:05:11.099 --> 00:05:14.419
is located in the center of his chest, just
like the heart that they have to shoot to

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:15.419
kill Chucky in the original.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:16.920
"Kill them all!"

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.580
"The heart!

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:20.060
Shoot him in the heart!"

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:28.479
After doing this, they toss him down the garbage
shoot, thinking that will be it.

00:05:28.479 --> 00:05:33.469
But like Child’s Play 1, 2, and 3, Chucky
always finds a way to come back whenever you

00:05:33.469 --> 00:05:34.710
think that he’s done for.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:38.129
And when he does, he kills the pervy IT guy
that put him back together.

00:05:38.129 --> 00:05:41.710
I guess in addition to watching Texas Chainsaw
movies with Chucky, they must have also been

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:42.979
watching some Saw.

00:05:42.979 --> 00:05:46.979
Chucky gets back into Andy’s life by mailing
himself to one of the other kids in Andy’s

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:51.020
building, which brings up the exact same question
I had in my video on Child’s Play 3: how

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:53.419
do you wrap a package if YOU’RE INSIDE OF
IIIIIITTTTT--

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:57.029
But this brings us to another interesting
parallel to the original, which is that Andy

00:05:57.029 --> 00:06:01.860
is the only one to realize that this is the
same Chucky as the one he had, and as a result,

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:03.740
everybody thinks Andy is crazy.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:07.860
The old Andy was put in the hospital, but
this one just goes all Anthony Rizzo on the

00:06:07.869 --> 00:06:08.869
TV.

00:06:08.869 --> 00:06:09.869
Could have just unplugged it.

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:10.879
All you had to do.

00:06:10.879 --> 00:06:14.719
There’s also a scene where Mrs. Norris goes
in a Kaslan car, which like Kaslan’s version

00:06:14.719 --> 00:06:17.800
of Uber, and Chucky takes control of it and
crashes it.

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:22.050
Remember, Mrs. Norris is the mother of Detective
Mike Norris, and in the original, Detective

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:26.160
Norris also gets his car crashed as a result
of Chucky, and the part that follows where

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:30.810
Chucky attacks from 360° around the car is
very similar in both movies.

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:34.550
The climax takes place in the store that Andy’s
Mom works at where they’re having the launch

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:39.469
of the brand new Buddi 2, which includes different
forms such as The Buddi Bear, an obvious Five

00:06:39.469 --> 00:06:42.319
Nights at Freddy Reference and the Leprechaun
outfit…

00:06:42.319 --> 00:06:44.970
I guess… possibly a Leprechaun reference…

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:49.020
But the idea of there being multiple Buddi
dolls being taken over by Chucky itself is

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:53.550
a reference to the previous movie in the franchise,
Cult of Chucky, where Charles Lee Ray manages

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.289
to get his soul into multiple bodies.

00:06:55.289 --> 00:06:59.369
I’ve heard this is an idea they wanted to
use for a long time, but didn’t, but if

00:06:59.369 --> 00:07:02.909
you think about it, it actually makes sense
here since Chucky is stated to have the ability

00:07:02.909 --> 00:07:04.899
to control all Kaslan products.

00:07:04.899 --> 00:07:09.759
Also, the RC police car that shouts out the
Robocop line could also be a nod towards Child’s

00:07:09.759 --> 00:07:14.639
Play 3 -- where one of the toys that Chucky
uses to attack Play Pals CEO Mr. Sullivan

00:07:14.639 --> 00:07:16.099
is this toy car.

00:07:16.099 --> 00:07:18.770
Those of you who watched my video on the original
Child’s Play…

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:21.550
I wonder how many times I said the word original
during this video….?

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:25.330
But those who saw it may remember my idea
to make a whole movie off the creepy mascot

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:27.069
from the Good Guy unveiling commercial.

00:07:27.069 --> 00:07:31.039
Well, in the new one, they use a creepy mascot
to during the unveiling of the actual product

00:07:31.039 --> 00:07:34.740
in stores -- and while it wasn’t a whole
movie, I was glad to see the mascot being

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:35.759
used for something.

00:07:35.759 --> 00:07:39.339
It’s no secret that one of the most beloved
scenes in the Child’s Play franchise is

00:07:39.339 --> 00:07:43.479
the final factory scene from Child’s Play
2, so to replicate some of that magic, the

00:07:43.479 --> 00:07:47.699
reboot throws Andy into a final confrontation
with Chucky in the warehouse at the back of

00:07:47.699 --> 00:07:51.729
the store, something that is alluded to earlier
on when Andy’s Mom blackmails her co-worker

00:07:51.729 --> 00:07:55.770
Wes, by threatening to tell his wife what
went on between him and a woman named Susan

00:07:55.770 --> 00:07:57.020
in the warehouse.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:00.949
Chucky kidnaps Andy’s Mom and tries to hang
her, which is how he killed the factory supervisor

00:08:00.949 --> 00:08:04.300
in Child’s Play 2, but Andy makes it just
in time to save her.

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:09.169
But as we know, and have established many
times, Chucky always finds a way to come back,

00:08:09.169 --> 00:08:13.080
and this time it’s Detective Norris with
the heroic one-liner where he says, “this

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:14.139
is the end.”

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.800
Very similar to OG Andy’s line.

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:20.040
“This is 
the end, friend.”

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:28.220
Except this time, it really is the end.

00:08:28.220 --> 00:08:29.460
Well… maybe not.

00:08:29.469 --> 00:08:33.470
The company Kaslan issues a statement where
they take no responsibility for the incident,

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:37.970
which parallels their PR response to their
stockholders in Child’s Play 2, and an evil

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:40.610
Buddi doll ends up on store shelves once more.

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:43.520
So the question about this ending is how did
Chucky survive?

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:46.770
We saw him get shot in the chest and his head
was pulled off.

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:47.920
There are a few possibilities.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:52.030
If they are trying to setup a sequel along
the lines of Child’s Play 2, it’s possible

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:54.850
that the company reconstructed Chucky to appease
their stockholders.

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:59.120
But I already covered why that’s a terrible
idea in my video on the second one, so another

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:03.000
possibility is that this simply wasn’t the
only one -- the disgruntled Vietnamese worker

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.350
could have made several rogue dolls for all
we know.

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:09.180
But my favorite theory is that because this
iteration of Chucky is connected to the cloud

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:13.450
and can interact with other Buddi dolls, it
could have sent it’s AI and everything that

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:18.160
it learned to other dolls, meaning Andy or
some unlucky kid could be up against a whole

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.740
army of Chuckys in the sequel.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:22.260
Let me know which theory you would get behind
in the comments.

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:26.900
I’ve gotten a lot of requests to cover Bride
of Chucky, Seed, Curse and Cult here on Things

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:30.830
You Missed, so with a sequel probably going
to happen now I’ll definitely have to do

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:31.830
those in the future.

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:36.080
So make sure you are subscribed to CZsWorld,
I post new horrors every week, just ring the

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:39.760
deathbell for notifications and I’ll see
you in the next one.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:41.710
Assuming we both survive.

